# Scope

Actual Claude Code 2.1.292, production ciel-runtime source at f87747a,
owned local provider fixture, fresh private HOME/config/workspace/temp and router ports.
No live router/session reset or private prompts copied. No production source edits.

## Evidence

- Harness: `native_sse_recovery.py` (accepts `--runtime-root` for installed retarget).
- Console: `console-source.txt`.
- Result: `run-claude-source-f87747a-152236/result.json`.
- Logs: `run-claude-source-f87747a-152236/router-combined.log`.
- Durable statuses: `run-claude-source-f87747a-152236/state/runtime-input-status.jsonl`.
- Native screen text: `run-claude-source-f87747a-152236/screen-latest.txt`.

### Observations

A fresh synthetic external SSE-shaped input was appended to the owned queue/status
with age 400 seconds. Only the owned launcher was temporarily suspended during
fixture publication and MCP calls to prevent delivery races; the router and native
CLI remained running. This does not establish a real transport failure.

Production `/ca/mcp` `recover_sse_delivery` status observed complete queue/history,
one stale request, compaction admission false and eligible true. Auto queued one
resumed restart to sole launcher 79220, request abbad0c1a7e1483f9f5592964aaaa111.
Second auto returned cooldown_active with 899.98 seconds remaining. Queue/history/
cursor bytes and mtimes were identical during the calls.

After owned launcher resumed, production control claimed the durable request,
terminated native child 82196 and launched native child 72176 with --continue,
renewing MCP launch and messaging socket. The restart request file was consumed.
Original request 1 reached the resumed CLI exactly once and transitioned
queued -> submitted -> replied. One socket injection and one fixture request
with the original as last user were observed. Original queue/history prefixes
were preserved. Teardown left no listener on the owned router port.

#### Capture limitation

PrintWindow was attempted against only the owned console; its rectangle was 0x0.
`native-screen-rendered.png` renders the captured native console text, not pixels.
The text contains the synthetic input, STUB-REPLY-4 and resumed notice response.
Actual pixel screenshot is unavailable in this console environment. Decisive
execution proof is the process identities, resume argv, MCP responses and logs.

# Boundary

Source-native acceptance passed. Parent then retargeted the harness to the
registry-installed f87747a; `run-claude-installed-f87747a-152529/result.json`
reports passed_native_sse_recovery and all ten checks true, including changed
native PID, --continue, consumed durable restart, original queued input replied
once, preserved queue/history prefixes and listener closed after teardown.
The public `sanitized-source-installed-results.json` retains both runs without
native command-line prompt bodies. Fixture age is synthetic; no upstream SSE
transport fault/reconnect is claimed.
